.TH OMX-DOMAIN 1 2026-11-18 omx-contract "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-domain \- open an OpenMixer contract domain and print a word or a range
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-domain
.I domain
.RI [ needs
.RI [ item
.RI [ name ]]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Opens the contract domain
.I domain
with libomx-domain and checks it. With only a domain it prints the domain's name; with an
.I item
it prints each word of that item; with a
.I name
it prints that word, or that parameter's minimum, maximum, default, unit and scale.
.I needs
is the version floor,
.IR x.y.z ,
the domain must meet; an empty one is none.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMX_CONTRACT_PATH
A directory holding
.IR domain / domain .json
to read instead of the installed contract directory. For tests and development only.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The item or the name is not in the domain.
.TP
.B 64
No domain was named.
.TP
.B 78
The domain is missing or invalid: the code of CONTRACT_CODES and the reason are printed on standard error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-contract (1)
